<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African April trade surplus 725 million rand.</title>
<headline>S.African April trade surplus 725 million rand.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa recorded a trade surplus of 725.00 million rand in April from a 1.98 billion rand surplus in March, latest South African Revenue Service figures show.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast the trade balance would show a 900 million rand surplus in April.  </p>
<p>	  (Data in billions of rand - rounded)</p>
<p>			  Apr '97	     Mar '97	    Apr '96</p>
<p>Exports		 11.29		 10.95		10.64</p>
<p>Imports		 10.57		  8.97		 9.88</p>
<p>Balance		  0.73		  1.98		 0.76</p>
<p>Cumulative totals:  Jan-Apr '97	 Jan-Apr '96</p>
<p>Exports		 42.32		 36.21</p>
<p>Imports		 39.55		 34.47</p>
<p>Balance		  2.77		  1.74</p>
<p>NOTE - This data covers the total foreign trade statistics of the common customs area of South Africa, Botswana, Lesotho, Namibia and Swaziland.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom (+27 11 482-1003)</p>
